// Engine-embedded `sys` interface, hand-maintained (decision D19). This file is the single definition of the
// `sys` module: its types, enums, `native type` declarations, relation types, and the `pub native fn` callables
// that the engine binds from its registry. It replaced the JSON catalogue, which SN4 deletes.
//
// Clause forms in use (sys-as-native section 2.4): `since`, `removed`, `formerly` and `spelling` on native
// callables; `key` and `availability` on relation types. Body-less `native fn` declarations are admitted only in
// engine-embedded modules (D12). Opaque identifiers are empty nominal bodies because the spec has no body-less
// opaque declaration (ORNA-NOMINAL-004).
//
// Design: docs/design/sys-as-native.md.

